# Scope: AI Integration Slice — Explained Simply

This is the same documentation as before, but every technical term is
explained in plain language as it comes up.

---

## 1. What This Is

A freelance designer can upload one or more messy client briefs (plain
text, PDF, or Word documents — up to 5 at once). Each file gets read by
an AI model (Google Gemini) in the background, and turned into a clean,
organized outline: a project name, a summary, goals, deliverables,
a timeline, budget notes, assumptions, and open questions.

Once that's done, the designer can click one button to "expand" the
outline into a fuller, more polished version — this second step uses a
different AI model (DeepSeek) instead of Gemini.

Both the original outline and the expanded version can be downloaded
as a PDF or Word document, generated automatically by the server.

**Logging in** works exactly the same as it did in the first slice
(Assessment 1) — nothing new was built here, the existing sign-up/
sign-in system was just reused. Every request checks that a user can
only see their own uploaded briefs, never anyone else's.

This slice deliberately does not let you edit results, share them with
someone else, or see a history of all your past briefs in one list.

